<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Parliament of Quillín</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1641</span> · Also known as Treaty of Quillín · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arauco-war">Arauco War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Parliament of Quillín was a peace meeting held in January 1641 between the Spanish governor of Chile, the Marquis of Baides, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mapuche">Mapuche</a> leaders. It recognised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/biobio-river">Biobío River</a> as the frontier between Spanish Chile and the independent Mapuche lands and allowed missionaries to work among them. It began a series of parlamentos that regulated relations between the two sides into the 19th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/parliament-of-quillin.jpg" alt="Parliament of Quillín" width="320" height="244" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alonso de Ovalle (1601-1651). Cartographe · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Parlamento_de_Quilin_1641_-_Alonso_de_Ovalle.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
